{"name":"Nevermore","hex":"#403940","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nevermore","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Never again; at no time in the future."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nevermore"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nevermore","blocks":[{"text":"Nevermore is an American heavy metal band formed in Seattle, Washington, in 1992. The band emerged following the dissolution of Sanctuary, whose final line-up included vocalist Warrel Dane, bassist Jim Sheppard and guitarist Jeff Loomis. The three musicians formed Nevermore with drummer Mark Arrington, who was replaced by Van Williams in 1994. Nevermore's music incorporates elements of progressive metal, thrash metal and power metal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Nevermore_Summerbreeze2007_04.jpg/330px-Nevermore_Summerbreeze2007_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevermore","wikidata":"Q130563"},{"title":"Nevermore (Mylène Farmer album)","blocks":[{"text":"Nevermore is the eighth live album by French singer Mylène Farmer, released on 27 September 2024 by Stuffed Monkey and distributed by Sony Music. It was recorded during concerts in June 2023 at the Groupama Stadium in Lyon during the concert tour of the same name. On the day of the album's premiere, the singer began the final stage of her tour, postponed in 2023 due to the riots in Paris. On 19 September, the official concert video for the song \"Oui mais... non\" was released."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Nevermore_%28Myl%C3%A8ne_Farmer_album%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevermore_(Myl%C3%A8ne_Farmer_album)","wikidata":"Q130479786"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Nevermore_Summerbreeze2007_06.jpg/500px-Nevermore_Summerbreeze2007_06